{
  "$comment": [
    "Block table for Minecraft Java Alpha v1.1.2 / v1.1.2_01.",
    "This file is checked in and compiled into the binary. The game ships",
    "knowing all of it -- players never extract or supply block data.",
    "Every numeric column was recovered once, by a maintainer, from an original",
    "client jar by tools/extract_blocks.py, and can be re-verified with",
    "--verify. The `name` column is ours: the alpha-era Block class carries no",
    "names at all. See docs/world-format.md and CONTRIBUTING.md.",
    "`texture` is the block's own atlas tile. `faces` is present only when the",
    "six sides differ, in the game's face order (0 -Y, 1 +Y, 2 -Z, 3 +Z, 4 -X,",
    "5 +X); when it is absent every face uses `texture`. Face textures that",
    "vary with metadata or with the surrounding world hold the no-metadata,",
    "no-neighbours answer -- run the extractor to have it name them. A negative",
    "value is the original's flag for a horizontally mirrored face (doors)."
  ],
